# ::tok “The amount of compensation is determined in each case individually and according to its circumstances,” says Adv. Reiff-Lignese, adding that “today most of the claims on the grounds of medical malpractice end with a compromise that weighs the chance and risk that each party has in conducting the procedure,” but the attorney added, saying that “there are cases in which the procedure is terminated only in a judgment, so if the claim is not rejected, the plaintiffs will receive full compensation for all their damages and for example “As part of a lawsuit conducted by our office, the District Court ruled that a minor caused cerebral palsy due to a delay in identifying fetal distress compensation in excess of ten million shekels.”
